al subcommands — an exact REPL-only name is told where the command lives (`/tokens`) and given the `yoyo -p "tokens"` escape hatch, and wiring those verbs as subcommands is separate work; a single word that resembles **nothing** (`zzqqx`) is still sent as a prompt, unchanged; and multi-word args (`yoyo do the thing`), flagged args, and `-p` are untouched byte-for-byte, because bare positional args as a prompt is a real feature.
